      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Some music videos have become very popular online. They sound very much like the works of the Singaporean singer "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Stefanie Sun",
            "zh": "孙燕姿"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But in fact, they were created through a piece of AI software called Sovits. Sovits is very easy to use. Its users can clone an “AI singer” with just a few "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "audio clips",
            "zh": "片段"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What do people think of this technology? Many, including some singers, are worried. This technology, they say, may make it harder to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "detect",
            "ref": "v-detect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fake",
            "ref": "v-fake"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " singing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What’s more, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "improper",
            "ref": "v-improper"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " use of “AI singers” may be "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "illegal",
            "ref": "v-illegal"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". “Some people use AI to clone a singer’s voice without his or her "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "permission",
            "ref": "v-permission"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They then put it on public display. This "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "violates",
            "ref": "v-violate"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the singer’s rights,” said lawyer Li Qiang. Even worse, some people may use “AI singers” for bad purposes."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On the other hand, “AI singers” can be used for good. The technology can “bring back” the voices of those who have passed away. For example, it can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "restore",
            "ref": "v-restore"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the voices of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "deceased",
            "zh": "死去的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " singers, such as "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Teresa Teng",
            "zh": "邓丽君"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and Michael Jackson. This can provide comfort to their fans and loved ones."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In addition, some musicians are open to “AI cloning”. Canadian singer Grimes is one of them. She says people are welcome to use AI to clone her voice for creative purposes. And some other singers are interested in how they may be able to work with AI. In short, an “AI singer” can be used for good or bad. It depends on the choice of the user. For this reason, regulations on related issues should be improved as soon as possible."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
